Subject: [PATCH] vmstatus: allow guest-pushed memory stats for guests without
 a balloon stats virtqueue (FreeBSD / OPNsense / pfSense)

PVE derives a VM's memory usage solely from the virtio-balloon stats
virtqueue (QemuServer.pm, ballooncb).  FreeBSD's vtballoon(4) attaches the
balloon device but never negotiates VIRTIO_BALLOON_F_STATS_VQ, so
query-balloon returns only `actual` and `max_mem`.  With total_mem/free_mem
missing, $d->{mem} keeps the cgroup value set earlier, which equals the whole
allocation -- the VM is permanently displayed at ~100% memory usage even
though the guest is nearly idle.

The upstream fix is freebsd-src PR #2509 ("virtio_balloon: Add memory
statistics queue support"), which is still open, targets main only, and would
require a custom OPNsense kernel.

This patch adds a fallback: if balloon stats are absent and a fresh stats file
has been written to /run/pve-bsdmem/<vmid>, use it.  The file is produced by
the pve-bsdmem helper via the QEMU guest agent.  Format is a single line:

    <unix_ts> <used_bytes> <free_bytes>

Entries older than 60s are ignored, so if the helper or the guest agent stops,
behaviour silently reverts to stock PVE.  No existing code path changes when
the guest does provide balloon stats.

Tested against: qemu-server 9.1.15 / pve-manager 9.2.2 (PVE 9.2.2)

--- a/usr/share/perl5/PVE/QemuServer.pm
+++ b/usr/share/perl5/PVE/QemuServer.pm
@@ -2651,7 +2651,23 @@
         if (defined($info->{total_mem}) && defined($info->{free_mem})) {
             $d->{mem} = $info->{total_mem} - $info->{free_mem};
             $d->{freemem} = $info->{free_mem};
-        }
+        } elsif (-r "/run/pve-bsdmem/$vmid") {
+            # Guest exposes no balloon stats virtqueue (FreeBSD/OPNsense), so the
+            # balloon reply carries only actual/max_mem and $d->{mem} would stay at
+            # the cgroup value (= full allocation).  Prefer stats pushed by
+            # pve-bsdmem, but only while they are fresh.
+            if (open(my $fh, '<', "/run/pve-bsdmem/$vmid")) {
+                my $line = <$fh>;
+                close($fh);
+                if (defined($line) && $line =~ m/^(\d+)\s+(\d+)\s+(\d+)\s*$/) {
+                    my ($ts, $used, $free) = ($1, $2, $3);
+                    if ((time() - $ts) < 60) {
+                        $d->{mem} = $used;
+                        $d->{freemem} = $free;
+                        $info->{bsdmem} = 1;
+                    }
+                }
+            }
+        }
 
         $d->{ballooninfo} = $info;
     };
